## Quicker-check artifacts — expensive-to-recreate outputs
The reproducibility bundle lets someone *re-run* an experiment; also save the outputs that are slow to
recreate so a reviewer, a fresh agent, or the verifier on a long run can *re-check* a result quickly
without rebuilding the pipeline: trained model weights/checkpoints, generated datasets, computed
operators/dictionaries, fitted-parameter files. Save under `results/data/` (or a campaign-appropriate
directory), keyed by the experiment label, and record their location in `results/INDEX.md`.

